# UIDAI certificate(s) used to check the digital signature on Aadhaar Secure QR codes.
#
# This file is intentionally empty of certificates. The app owner must add them:
#   1. Go to https://uidai.gov.in -> Ecosystem / Developer section -> "UIDAI certificate details"
#      (the certificate for Secure QR code / offline e-KYC signature verification).
#   2. Download the current certificate(s). If a certificate is in binary .cer/DER form, convert it:
#        openssl x509 -inform der -in uidai.cer -out uidai.pem
#   3. Paste each certificate below, including the -----BEGIN CERTIFICATE----- and
#      -----END CERTIFICATE----- lines. Keep old certificates while older QR codes are still in use.
#
# With no certificate here, Second Look still reads the QR but reports that its signature wasn't checked.
# Lines outside BEGIN/END blocks (like these) are ignored.
